{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>He crouched, lay down like a lion, and like a lioness — who will rouse him?</b> Above it said: \"Behold, a people like a lioness rises, and like a lion lifts itself up.\" Above, lioness preceded, for so is the way: at first he grows strong a little like a lioness, and afterward lifts himself higher and higher like a lion, which grows ever stronger. Here, however, lion preceded lioness, alluding also: \"lay down like a lion\" in the days of Moses, \"and like a lioness\" in the days of Joshua — for the face of Moses is like the face of the sun, and the face of Joshua is like the face of the moon." "<b>Those who bless you — blessed; and those who curse you — cursed.</b> Balaam, who intended in his heart to curse them — therefore he concluded with a curse. And Isaac, in his blessings of \"may El give you,\" [said] \"cursed be those who curse you, and blessed be those who bless you.\" Therefore Balak did not say to him to curse them anymore, but said to him: \"Flee for yourself.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:04.716199672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}